---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contact = "hello@trydrft.app";
const label = "text-[10px] tracking-[0.28em] uppercase";
const h2 = "mt-14 text-[1.125rem] leading-snug font-light text-ink";
const p = "mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mut";
const ul = "mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mut";
const a = "text-pt underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-ink";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy · drft"
  description="What drft collects, why, and who helps run it."
>
  <main>
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between px-6 pt-10 sm:px-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-[13px] tracking-[0.5em] text-pt uppercase">drft</a>
      <a href="/?signin" class="text-sm text-mut transition-colors hover:text-ink">Sign in</a>
    </div>

    <article class="mx-auto max-w-[36rem] px-6 pt-24 pb-28 sm:pt-32">
      <p class:list={["text-pl", label]}>Effective October 28, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-[clamp(1.75rem,4vw,2.25rem)] leading-[1.15] font-extralight tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class={p}>
        drft is a space for unfinished thoughts. This page explains what we collect, why, and the
        few services that help us run drft. Questions go to <a class={a} href={`mailto:${contact}`}
          >{contact}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Your account</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        You sign in with Apple, Google, or GitHub through Clerk, our authentication provider. We
        receive your email address and an account identifier. With Apple, we ask only for your email,
        not your name, and Hide My Email relay addresses work. Google and GitHub may also share your
        name and profile photo with Clerk; drft doesn't use them.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>What you create</h2>
      <ul class={ul}>
        <li>— The text of your thoughts, and any notes you add to them.</li>
        <li>— The closing line you write when you set a thought to rest.</li>
        <li>— When each of these was created, and which connections you dismissed.</li>
        <li>— Your settings: the daily email's send time, your timezone, and your email address.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class={p}>All of this is stored by Convex, which hosts drft's backend and database.</p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Connections and OpenAI</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Only if you allow connections, the text of each thought is sent to OpenAI's API to create an
        embedding — a set of numbers drft uses to find related thoughts. Nothing else about you is
        sent. OpenAI does not use API data to train its models, and may retain it for up to 30 days
        for abuse monitoring.
      </p>
      <p class={p}>
        Thoughts you capture before deciding aren't sent. If you allow connections later, those
        thoughts are sent then, so they can be connected too.
      </p>
      <p class={p}>
        You can turn connections off anytime in settings. That stops new thoughts from being sent;
        connections already found stay.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>The daily email</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Resend delivers the daily email. It receives your email address and that day's thought.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>The website and web app</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Vercel hosts the website and web app. Vercel Web Analytics collects aggregated, cookieless
        page-view analytics on them.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>The iPhone app</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Dictation uses Apple's on-device speech recognition; the audio never leaves your device.
        Microphone and speech recognition permission is used only for dictation.
      </p>
      <p class={p}>
        The app keeps a queue of captures not yet sent and a cache of your collection on the device.
        The cache is cleared when you sign out.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul class={ul}>
        <li>— No ads.</li>
        <li>— No tracking across other apps or websites.</li>
        <li>— No selling or sharing your data for advertising.</li>
        <li>— No data brokers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2}>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        We keep your data while your account exists. To delete your account and all associated
        data, email <a class={a} href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>; we'll confirm and delete
        it. To access or export your data, write to the same address.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Children</h2>
      <p class={p}>drft is not directed at children under 13.</p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Changes</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new effective
        date.
      </p>
    </article>

    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>
